[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Log parsers high-level requirements
UID: FMD-HLR-PRS
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-20
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
High-level requirements of the log parsers item (PRS), written from the code as built. The item is the six
modules `ulog_parser.py`, `ardupilot_parser.py`, `ardupilot_text_parser.py`, `mavlink_telemetry_parser.py`,
`betaflight_parser.py` and `dji_parser.py` under `flightmd_core/services/`. Each turns one log file into the
internal form (topics, parameters, flight metadata). Low-level requirements are in `llr-prs.sdoc`, the design in
`06-design/lld-prs.md`, the input formats in `03-system/icd/icd-log-formats.md`. Where the code does less than
its system requirement asks, the requirement states what the code does and the gap is listed in the design,
section 6.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Common interface and internal form

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: One parser interface
STATEMENT: >>>
Each parser class (`ULogParser`, `ArduPilotBinParser`, `ArduPilotTextParser`, `MavlinkTelemetryParser`,
`BetaflightParser`, `DJIParser`) shall offer `parse(path)` that returns a tuple of topics (a dict of topic name
to pandas DataFrame), parameters (a dict of name to float) and one `FlightMetadata`, and shall raise
`FileNotFoundError` when the path does not exist.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: One log-relative clock in microseconds
STATEMENT: >>>
Every topic shall carry a `timestamp` column in microseconds on a clock that is zero at the start of the log.
The source clock is: PX4 ULog, the logger's boot clock minus the ULog start timestamp; dataflash, `TimeUS`
(or `TimeMS` x 1000) minus the earliest time seen; telemetry log, vehicle boot time aligned to the ground
station receive clock, minus the earliest sample; blackbox, the main-frame `time` field with the 32-bit
rollover removed, minus the first accepted main frame; DJI, the index of the latest OSD record x 100 000.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: PX4 names and units for the shared columns
STATEMENT: >>>
The parsers shall use these names and units wherever the source log holds the quantity:
`vehicle_gps_position.lat` and `.lon` in degrees x 1e7, `.alt` in millimetres, `.hdop` as a plain ratio,
`.eph` and `.epv` in metres, `.fix_type` on the 0 to 6 scale with 3 meaning a 3D fix;
`battery_status.voltage_v` in volts, `.current_a` in amperes, `.remaining` from 0 to 1, `.temperature` in
degrees Celsius, `.voltage_cell_v[k]` in volts; `vehicle_angular_velocity` and `vehicle_rates_setpoint` in
rad/s; `sensor_accel` in m/s^2; `vehicle_status.arming_state` with 2 for armed and 1 for disarmed and
`.nav_state` in PX4 numbering; `vehicle_land_detected.landed` as a boolean.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Instances of the same sensor
STATEMENT: >>>
When a log holds several instances of one sensor (IMU, battery, GPS receiver, EKF core), the first instance
shall be stored under the bare topic name and each other instance under `<name>_<instance number>`, with no
row of one instance mixed into another.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parse progress
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser.parse`, `ArduPilotBinParser.parse`, `ArduPilotTextParser.parse` and `MavlinkTelemetryParser.parse`
shall accept an optional `progress` callable and call it during the parse with the fraction done, a number
from 0 to 1. `BetaflightParser.parse` and `DJIParser.parse` take no such argument and report no progress.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: No limits inside the parsers
STATEMENT: >>>
The parsers shall apply no size, row-count or time limit of their own. `BetaflightParser` and `DJIParser` read
the whole file into memory; the other parsers read through pyulog or pymavlink and hold every wanted sample in
memory. Bounding the work is left to the caller (file size limit and parser process time limit).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
As built. SYS-003 allocates the limits to intake, report and api; this requirement records that the parsers
depend on them and add none.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test exercises a limit inside a parser because there is none. A review checks that no parser truncates,
samples or stops on size, and that the caller runs the parse in a process it can stop.
<<<
ALLOCATION: parsers
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: PX4 ULog

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog topics
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser` shall read a PX4 ULog through pyulog, load by default only the 17 topics the analysers use, give
the data of renamed topics (`angular_velocity`, `sensor_gps`) under their older names
(`vehicle_angular_velocity`, `vehicle_gps_position`), put the estimator instance that was primary for most of
the log under the bare `estimator_*` names, give GPS position as degrees x 1e7 and millimetres whichever
field names the firmware logged, and cut `esc_status` down to the ESCs that exist.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog parameters and metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser` shall return the log's initial parameters as floats and metadata holding: duration in seconds from
the ULog first and last timestamps, firmware version and board from the info messages, the PX4 release decoded
from `ver_sw_release`, airframe id and name from `SYS_AUTOSTART`, vehicle type from `vehicle_status`, the UTC
start time from the first GPS time later than 2010, the number of arming events, the flight modes used, and
maximum altitude, maximum horizontal speed and distance flown from `vehicle_local_position`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog parse warnings
STATEMENT: >>>
`ULogParser` shall add a parse warning when pyulog reports file corruption and a parse warning giving the
number and total length of logger dropouts. It adds no warning for topics, parameters or values it leaves out
or fills in.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: ArduPilot dataflash, binary and text

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash messages to topics
STATEMENT: >>>
`ArduPilotBinParser` (binary, through pymavlink `DFReader_binary`) and `ArduPilotTextParser` (text, through
`DFReader_text`, same mapping) shall read the IMU, BAT, BCL, GPS, GPA, ESC, VIBE, XKF4, NKF4, RATE and POWR
message families and the MODE, MSG, EV and ARM messages, and produce `vehicle_angular_velocity`,
`sensor_accel`, `battery_status`, `vehicle_gps_position`, `esc_status`, `vibration`, `ekf_test_ratios`,
`vehicle_rates_setpoint`, `system_power`, `vehicle_status` and `vehicle_land_detected` with the units of
HLR-PRS-003. All other message types are ignored.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash arming, mode and landed state
STATEMENT: >>>
The dataflash parsers shall build `vehicle_status` from ARM messages, or from EV events 10 (armed) and 11
(disarmed) when the log has no ARM message, and from MODE messages; shall leave `arming_state` out when the
log holds neither; shall map the ArduPilot mode name to the nearest PX4 `nav_state` or to no value; and shall
build `vehicle_land_detected` from EV events 18 (land complete) and 28 (not landed).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash parameters and metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
The dataflash parsers shall return the numeric parameters the reader collected, and metadata holding: duration
from the earliest and latest message time, the firmware banner and the vehicle type taken from it, the board
name from the board identity banner, the frame name from the frame parameters or the "Frame:" banner, the UTC
start time from the GPS week and millisecond of the first 3D fix, the arm count and the mode names used.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataflash parsers give no parse warnings
STATEMENT: >>>
The dataflash parsers shall return an empty `parse_warnings` list. Bytes the reader could not decode, messages
with no time field, rows dropped for missing values and modes with no PX4 equivalent are not reported.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
As built. This is less than SYS-005 and SAF-004 ask; it is recorded as a defect in `06-design/lld-prs.md`
section 6.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test checks the warning list of a dataflash parse. A review checks that `ArduPilotBinParser.parse` never
passes `parse_warnings` to `FlightMetadata`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: No guessed estimator status for ArduPilot and telemetry logs
STATEMENT: >>>
The dataflash and telemetry-log parsers shall not produce an `estimator_status` topic. They shall give the
estimator innovation test ratios in `ekf_test_ratios`, squaring the values ArduPilot logs so that 1.0 means
rejected as it does on PX4, together with the status words as logged.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
ArduPilot and MAVLink status bits do not match PX4's `innovation_check_flags` and `solution_status_flags`. A
mapped bit mask would give estimator findings that look exact and are not.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: MAVLink telemetry log

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: One vehicle from a shared link
STATEMENT: >>>
`MavlinkTelemetryParser` shall keep only the messages of one system id and component id: the pair that sent
the most HEARTBEATs with an autopilot type other than "invalid" (8) and a vehicle type other than ground
station (6). It shall add a parse warning with the number of messages ignored from other senders. When the log
holds no such HEARTBEAT it shall use the messages of every sender, produce no `vehicle_status`, and add a parse
warning saying so.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Telemetry log clock
STATEMENT: >>>
`MavlinkTelemetryParser` shall time each sample by the vehicle's own boot time where the message carries one,
shifted by the median offset between receive time and boot time, and by the ground station receive time where
it does not. It shall add a parse warning when no message carried a vehicle time and a parse warning with the
number of vehicle reboots (boot clock going back by more than 1 s).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Telemetry messages to topics
STATEMENT: >>>
`MavlinkTelemetryParser` shall read the 28 message types of `WANTED_TYPES` through pymavlink and produce
`vehicle_angular_velocity`, `sensor_accel`, `battery_status`, `vehicle_gps_position`,
`vehicle_global_position`, `esc_status`, `vibration` (ArduPilot) or `vehicle_imu_status` (PX4),
`ekf_test_ratios`, `system_power`, `vehicle_status` and `vehicle_land_detected`, converting milli-g, mV, cA,
cV, centi-degrees Celsius, percent and millimetre fields to the units of HLR-PRS-003 and treating the MAVLink
"unknown" sentinel values as missing.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Telemetry arming, mode, parameters and metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
`MavlinkTelemetryParser` shall take the arming state from the HEARTBEAT armed flag (bit 128 of `base_mode`),
the `nav_state` from the HEARTBEAT custom mode of a PX4 or ArduPilot autopilot, the landed state from
EXTENDED_SYS_STATE, the parameters from PARAM_VALUE (decoding PX4 integer parameters from their bytes), and
metadata holding duration, the UTC start time from the receive clock when it is later than 2010, firmware,
board, vehicle type, airframe, arm count and modes used.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Unreadable telemetry is counted
STATEMENT: >>>
`MavlinkTelemetryParser` shall count the chunks of the stream that pymavlink could not decode and add a parse
warning with the count.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Betaflight and INAV blackbox

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox decoding
STATEMENT: >>>
`BetaflightParser` shall decode a blackbox log with its own decoder: the "H name:value" header lines, I and P
main frames, S slow frames, G and H GPS frames and E events, with field encodings 0, 1, 3, 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10
and predictors 0 to 11 as the header declares them, for data versions 1 and 2. It shall raise `ValueError` with
a message when the file has no blackbox header, no field definitions, definitions it cannot use, or no
decodable main frame.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Damaged blackbox data and several logs in one file
STATEMENT: >>>
`BetaflightParser` shall skip a frame that fails to decode, is not followed by another frame, or jumps by more
than 5000 loop iterations or 10 s from the frame before it, carry on from the next frame it can trust, and add
a parse warning with the number of frames skipped. When the file holds several logs it shall analyse the
largest one with field definitions and add a parse warning naming which. A file that ends in the middle of a
frame is decoded up to that point with no warning.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox fields to topics
STATEMENT: >>>
`BetaflightParser` shall produce `vehicle_angular_velocity` and `vehicle_rates_setpoint` in rad/s,
`sensor_accel` in m/s^2, `actuator_outputs` as logged, `esc_status` in mechanical rpm, `battery_status` in
volts and amperes and `vehicle_gps_position` in degrees x 1e7 and millimetres. It shall leave out the
accelerometer when the header has no `acc_1G`, and the battery when the voltage unit of the firmware is not
known, each with a parse warning.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox arming, parameters and metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
For Betaflight 3.5 and later `BetaflightParser` shall build `vehicle_status` from the arm switch (bit 0) and
the angle and horizon switches (bits 1 and 2) of the slow-frame and flight-mode-event flags and from disarm
events; for INAV and older firmware it shall produce no `vehicle_status`. It shall return the numeric header
values as parameters, and metadata holding duration, the firmware revision line, the board line, the UTC start
time from "Log start datetime" when later than 2010, the arm count and the modes used.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: DJI flight record

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI record decoding
STATEMENT: >>>
`DJIParser` shall read a DJI app flight record from its prefix, record area and details block for the layouts
of versions 1 to 5, 6 to 11, 12 and 13 or later, remove the per-record XOR scrambling of version 7 and later,
and decode the OSD, HOME, GIMBAL, RC, CUSTOM, DEFORM, CENTER_BATTERY, SMART_BATTERY and SMART_BATTERY_GROUP
records. It shall raise `ValueError` with a message for a DJI aircraft .DAT file, a file shorter than 100
bytes, a damaged header, records that run past the end of the file, and a record with no readable OSD data.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI records to topics
STATEMENT: >>>
`DJIParser` shall produce `vehicle_gps_position` (degrees x 1e7; altitude in millimetres as height above
take-off plus the home altitude), `vehicle_local_position` (metres and m/s, z down), `vehicle_attitude`
(radians and a quaternion), `vehicle_status` (armed when the motors are on), `vehicle_land_detected`,
`battery_status`, `manual_control_setpoint`, `dji_gimbal` and `dji_deform`, each sample timed by the OSD
record before it at 100 ms per OSD record. It returns no parameters and no firmware version, and sets the
vehicle type to "Copter".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI key exchange for version 13 and later
STATEMENT: >>>
For a record of version 13 or later `DJIParser` shall send one HTTPS POST to
`https://dev.dji.com/openapi/v1/flight-records/keychains` holding the record's wrapped key material (the
KeyStorage records), the auxiliary version and department numbers, and the DJI developer key from the
environment variable `DJI_API_KEY` in the `Api-Key` header; no flight data, position or file name is sent. It
shall use the returned AES keys to decrypt the records, wait at most 30 s, read at most 4 MiB of reply, follow
no redirect, and raise `ValueError` with the reason when the service cannot be reached or refuses.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-027
STATUS: Active
TITLE: No DJI request offline or without a key
STATEMENT: >>>
`DJIParser` shall make no network request when the environment variable `FLIGHTMD_OFFLINE` is `1`, `true`,
`yes` or `on` (any letter case) or when `DJI_API_KEY` is empty or unset. In either case a record of version 13
or later is refused with a `ValueError` that names both variables. Records of version 12 and earlier never
cause a request.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-028
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI parse warnings
STATEMENT: >>>
`DJIParser` shall add a parse warning with the number of damaged records it skipped and a parse warning with
the number of records it could not decrypt. It adds no warning for a record that is too short for its type,
for OSD records dropped for an impossible position, or for a missing home altitude.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-029
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
`DJIParser` shall return metadata holding: duration as (number of OSD records - 1) x 0.1 s, the UTC start time
from the details block or else from the first CUSTOM record, the aircraft model name from the OSD drone type,
the arm count, the DJI flight mode names used, and maximum height above take-off and maximum horizontal speed.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Helpers given to format detection

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-PRS-030
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Content checks for blackbox and DJI files
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall give format detection three content checks: `looks_like_blackbox` (the blackbox product line is
in the header), `looks_like_dji_dat` (a DJI aircraft .DAT signature) and `check_dji_txt` (the header starts
like a DJI flight record: yes, no, or too short to tell), and the fixed refusal text `DAT_UNSUPPORTED`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parsers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[[/SECTION]]
